{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213422,"nonce":"7uwh8Nu1r2cIU1gNsWZjqHnhDYE=","title":"Lua 5.4 and a Python dialect as Zyntax front-ends","message":"A dynamic object model in HIR: member get and set, invoke, index,\nmetatables, descriptors, compiled to the core object protocol with inline\ncaches keyed on descriptor epochs. Then a Lua 5.4 grammar (coroutines as\ntasks) and a Python dialect (generators and async as krio-async state\nmachines).\n\nNative access for both is the plugin ABI and nothing else: no ffi.cdef, no\nC-API extension modules; a spoke sees only the descriptors its driver grants.\nLua 5.4 can be faithful; Python is a dialect and is presented as one.\n\nGate: the plugin from the bundle phase callable from Zyntax-hosted Lua with\nno plugin changes.","files":null}]}